 {"id":"fabro-ee2c","title":"Require ml record for implementer near-miss tool lessons","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:36:46.111Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:36:46.111Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md step 6 (or the stage-journal hook), make ml record mandatory for near-miss tool lessons. implementer@1's edit_file old_string swallowed a whole test loop body in fib_test.go, was caught only by re-reading, and the lesson went into the run journal that no future session loads; implementer@2 then spent 284 s / 0.49 USD (42% of run agent cost) editing the same 1,100-line table-literal file without the guardrail. Expected effect: the next implementer inherits the scoped-old_string guardrail via ml prime --files.","labels":["revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-169b","title":"Declare lesson_capture in the implementer node's context_allow_keys","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:38.461Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T07:56:24.008Z","description":"Seed fabro-f831 makes lesson_capture a required key of the Implemented JSON in .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md, but workflow.fabro's implementer node still declares context_allow_keys=implementation_summary,journal, so the undeclared key drops as drift on every future pass (per fabro-900e comment). Change: one line in workflow.fabro implementer node — context_allow_keys=implementation_summary,lesson_capture,journal; optionally also add it to the reviewer's preamble_allow_keys. Effect: the enforced record-or-skip answer lands durably instead of being discarded.","labels":["revision"],"closedAt":"2026-09-05T07:56:24.008Z","closeReason":"Closed 2026-09-05 triage: lesson_capture already declared in implementer context_allow_keys (workflow.fabro line 106)."}
 {"id":"fabro-3d2d","title":"Add a repo-layout map to the planner prompt or AGENTS.md","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:38.588Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:38.588Z","description":"planner@1 burned 354.7 s / $0.219 of the $0.547 total (50,460 input tokens) on ~10 exploratory calls just to locate dev-loop assets that live at .fabro/workflows/develop/ in the same repo; planner@2 with the layout in context took 98 s / $0.064. Change: add a 5-line Repo layout section to AGENTS.md (loaded as memory into every stage) or .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md: gofib at repo root; dev-loop assets at .fabro/workflows/develop/; reviews at .fabro/reviews/; journals at .fabro/journal/. Effect: first planner pass drops from ~6 min toward ~100 s — roughly −4.5 min wall and −$0.15 per run. Distinct from the sd call-economy seeds (fabro-e4fa/f4cd/1399): those tune tracker calls, this removes filesystem orientation calls.","labels":["revision"]}
-{"id":"fabro-4b57","title":"Emit a loop-work diff in evidence.nu when only churn files changed","status":"in_progress","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:44.453Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T16:21:43.927Z","description":"Seeds targeting .fabro/ paths are classified as loop churn by .fabro/workflows/develop/scripts/evidence.nu, so captures read seed-work=0 files +0/-0 and reviewers must run their own git diff. Change: in evidence.nu, when seed_rows is empty but churn_rows is not, emit the per-seed (claim-base) diff of changed loop files under a loop-work diff section — the per-seed diff-base machinery from fabro-1e9f's theme already provides the base. Effect: reviews of dev-loop seeds verify from context, removing the per-review git detour. Cross-ref: fabro-1e9f (diff against last seed boundary) is the same machinery at run level.","labels":["revision"]}
